lines += ['```','', 'The first counts attempt failed with no space left on device creating a local product directory. Root had zero available space, with 14 GB of disposable local product artifacts. Moved only that cache directory to the named scratch path and removed it, recovering 14 GB; source and review evidence were preserved. The failed attempt wrote no count table. Retried regeneration once successfully: counts-update-disk-full.log and results-disk-full.json retain the failure; counts-update.log retains the successful 129.911-second run.', '', 'The initial full command-package run could not find warmed archives because driver tests set temporary XDG_CACHE_HOME values. Retried the full package with ADAMIC_BUILD_CACHE_DIR=/home/agent/.cache/adamic-build explicitly inherited, as Loom supplies a fixed shared product directory. It passed without any test or compiler code change. Both attempts are retained, not counted as mutants.','','## Exact validation commands and results','','| Label | Command | Exit | Wall seconds | Max reported test seconds |','| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for r in results:
 lines.append('| '+r['label']+' | `'+ ' '.join(r['command'])+'` | '+str(r['exit'])+' | '+str(r['seconds'])+' | '+str(max((t['seconds'] for t in r['tests']),default=0))+' |')
lines += ['', 'Corrected full command run: env ADAMIC_BUILD_CACHE_DIR=/home/agent/.cache/adamic-build timeout 180 go test ./cmd/adamic/... -count=1 -timeout 90s -parallel 4 -p 1 -json. Exit 0; cmd-adamic-shared-cache.log records the complete run.', '', 'Explicit guard: timeout 120 go test ./internal/ir -run ^TestCallTargetReaders$ -count=1 -timeout 90s -json. Exit 0; reader-guard.log records it. gofmt -l output is empty. Source whitespace checks exclude historical review artifacts; inherited patch and log bytes are retained.', '', f'Final accepted runs contain {len(passed)} pass events and {len(skipped)} skip events, with zero failing events. Pass counts include nested test events and setup/product tests, not just independent leaves. Skips are listed in all-test-events.json; opt-in WASI and platform-only cases are not claimed as executed. The initial cache failures are excluded from this accepted-run total and described above. No complete repository gate, ahra invocation or Loom submission was run.','','## Fresh a-check and mutant evidence','',f'Built this branch\'s compiler with timeout 120 go build -o /workspace/scratch/hidden-ac-m-compiler ./cmd/adamic, then ran timeout 180 python3 review/compiler/loom-r-hidden-boundaries-ac-m/a_check.py. The unchanged pinned Gate.aCheck at fbac28c62493f27a788edc02a18bc8edb68de5da accepts all 60 changed programs: {dict(status_counts)}. Every program is byte-identical to the original supplied tip. Both removed-header and wrong-reason mutants fail, using real compiler diagnostics, and the header is restored. See a-check-statuses.json, a-check.json and a-check-mutants.json.', '', 'Ran timeout 840 python3 review/compiler/loom-r-hidden-boundaries-ac-m/mutants.py. The original 38 compiler overlays and four flow harness mutants all exit 1 at test assertions; the harness exits 0. No mutant is credited for a Go build failure, C compiler error, Werror or timeout. All copied Go mutant sources are .go.txt and cannot enter normal builds. The original patch sources remain referenced under review/compiler/hidden-boundaries-next/getters; this pass writes only new evidence.','','| Mutant | Catching failed tests |','| --- | --- |']
